Z||000002||sqoach||11-13-2001||02:33 PM||||Hey, looks just like mine!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>(except I have cooler pedals)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>My clutch pedal is about 1/4" below my brake pedal. Anyone care to hook me up with a non-bent pedal?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif">              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">               <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||11-13-2001||02:51 PM||||That's not where the bend occurs. The problem with the clutch pedal is more of a twist rather than a bend. Actually that looks like a rather neat modification, as I've been known to hit the brake pedal whilst pushing in the clutch.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||11-13-2001||03:01 PM||||Phil--I know you have a steel pedal.  Take a look at yours again.  Are you sure that's not what yours looks like?  That looks almost identical to mine.  I have steel and it's not bent (AFAIK).<P>Triad--Your pedal is probably OK as long as the clutch pedal face is the same angle as the brake.  Follow what I'm saying?  It's hard to think when you're tired.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||TRiAD||11-13-2001||03:18 PM||||MM ~ I get it...you're saying this is how they're <I>supposed</I> to look, right?<P>Well, I don't have anything to compare it to...can someone post a pic of a "good" one?<P><I>Man, and I was really hoping this would get me back on the road for Saturday's NIFE meeting...</I>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Archie||11-13-2001||03:25 PM||||The part of the pedal that bends is the "U" shaped bracket as shown in these pics.<P>This pic is a bent AL. pedal... see how the "U" bracket is bent in at the top.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-593s_1.jpg"> <P>This pedal is a good steel one and you can see how the bracket is nice and square.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-594s_1.jpg"> <P>The bending of that bracket on the AL pedal causes the Banjo pin (on the left) to move closer to the pedal pivot thus reducing the effective travel of the banjo and the hyd. system.<P>The bend you illustrate in your pics. has nothing to do with the AL bent pedal thing we discussed.<P>Archie<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||XDrewX||11-13-2001||03:27 PM||||had to edit because Archie was answering my question as I was typing it.<P>New question:<P>On the new replacement pedal, I know the u bracket is steel, but is the "leg" steel also?<P>Thanks<P>Andrew <BR><p>[This message has been edited by XDrewX (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||TRiAD||11-13-2001||04:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>The part of the pedal that bends is the "U" shaped bracket as shown in these pics.<P>...see how the "U" bracket is bent in at the top... <P>...This pedal is a good steel one and you can see how the bracket is nice and square...<P><BR>The bending of that bracket on the AL pedal causes the Banjo pin (on the left) to move closer to the pedal pivot thus reducing the effective travel of the banjo and the hyd. system.<P>The bend you illustrate in your pics. has nothing to do with the AL bent pedal thing we discussed.<P>Archie<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OK, I went back and looked at mine, now that I kinda know what I'm looking for. <P>If my "U" is bent, it's kinda slight, and it's bent "out" not "in", would this have the same effect?<P>Thanks!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||sqoach||11-13-2001||05:02 PM||||So what part of my pedal would be bent for it to be slightly lower than the brake pedal? In my other fiero, the clutch pedal is higher than the brake pedal.||||reg||5
Z||000010||MrPBody||11-13-2001||08:34 PM||||sqoach --<P>I guess the "U" could be twisted back toward you.  I haven't seen this in person, but maybe it could happen.  Or you might have a <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/015204.html" TARGET=_blank>short pushrod</A>.  (Nothing personal.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>Yep, the twisted clutch pedal lever looks normal.  (Fiero normal)  I think they're twisted to clear the wheelwell hump.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Archie||11-14-2001||02:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MrPBody:<BR><B>sqoach --<P>I guess the "U" could be twisted back toward you.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's exactly right..... on most (but not all) bent Alum. pedals the "U" shaped bracket will also be bent back toward the driver a bit. That is what has some people comparing pedal heights. <P>BTW, I have seen a lot of bent pedals that were not bent back toward the driver, so the pedal height comparison is not always the best way to check for a bad pedal.<P>You can see how it's bent back in this picture.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-595s.jpg"> <P>BTW..... I bet that I've replaced 75 or 80 pedals in the last 15 years and I've never seen one bent outboard.<P>Archie<P>P.S. Do you remember when Clinton was campaigning for his first term? The people running the campaign realized that the hot ticket issue at that time was the economy. Whenever the campaign started to go off track they had a phrase they used among themselves to keep on issue. They used to say "It's the Economy Stupid!" As much as I've advocated (for several years) the replacement of the old clutch pedals, and with 4 or 5 current threads going on with this topic. Sometimes I just want to SCREAM "IT'S THE PEDAL STUPID!!!!" <P>Archie<P>------------------<BR>Just how fast do you want to go?||||reg||1
Z||000012||revin||11-14-2001||07:28 AM||||TRiAD- Haveing fun with your new car? Much different than photoshop huh.||||reg||7
Z||000013||TRiAD||11-14-2001||10:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by revin:<BR><B>TRiAD- Haveing fun with your new car? Much different than photoshop huh.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Heh.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Actually, I've done several project cars in the past (mostly VWs and Hondas) and know it's harder than photoshop, but PS makes for good motivation. <P>This wouldn't be such a setback if I weren't tapped at the moment and if I had other transportation.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
